[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Step 130 -- Epoch-resolved axis trajectory on the pooled
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   independent dual-leg record.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Steps 127-128 established that both eras carry lapse-slip anomalies
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   in the raw astrometric record on zero-Warsaw-lineage fits -- but at
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   different sky positions and on different legs: the pre-2018 record
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   carries the registered inbound-leg anomaly at the declared axis
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   (34,-13), while the post-2017 record carries a same-class anomaly at
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   the displaced axis (120,-40) on the outbound leg.  The boundary
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   channel's registered position is therefore epoch-dependent, and two
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   readings remain:
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   * dynamic-field -- the boundary structure moved: the anomalous
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   direction drifts continuously from the declared toward the
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   displaced orientation as transit epoch advances;
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   * era-artifact / sharp switch -- two unrelated era-locked
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   structures; no continuous trajectory connects them.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   This step discriminates on the pooled independent record: every
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   dual-leg comet from the step-127 (pre-2018) and step-128 (post-2017)
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   refits, each carrying an independently fitted leg-disagreement
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   carrier (our_ddirf), a leg-rotation channel (our_drot), the
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   single-fit inbound-leg deviation (reconstructed per-comet as
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   sep(boundary-leg aphelion, osculating periapsis)), and the
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   boundary-leg aphelion direction for cap classification at any axis.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Perihelion year is used as the epoch proxy; the boundary-transit
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   epochs bracket perihelion (inbound tens of years before, outbound
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   tens of years after) and co-move with it on the ~75-year baseline
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   spanned here.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Registered tests
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   T1  per-bin contrasts: fixed epoch bins; in-cap vs out-of-cap
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Mann-Whitney on ddirf at the declared and displaced axes.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   T2  arc-trajectory scan: per bin, the cap-contrast gap profiled
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   along the declared->displaced great-circle arc (s in
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   [-0.5, 1.5]); the argmax position per bin is the epoch's
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   measured axis position on the arc.  Trajectory statistic:
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   Spearman(bin epoch, s_argmax).  Null: epoch-label permutation
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   re-deriving the full trajectory (500).
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   T3  drift-vs-switch model comparison on the pooled cohort: the
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   cap contrast under (a) the fixed declared axis, (b) the fixed
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   displaced axis, (c) the best switch model -- declared cap
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   before T_s, displaced cap after -- and (d) the best drift
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   model -- a slerp-interpolated axis sweeping declared->
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   displaced over a ramp (T_c, W).  The switch/drift advantage
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   over the best fixed axis is evaluated against an epoch-label
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   permutation null (500); fixed axes are unaffected by the
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   permutation, so the null prices exactly the epoch-ordering
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   component.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   T4  epoch interaction within caps: Spearman(yr, ddirf) among
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   declared-cap and displaced-cap members separately, with
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   label-shuffle nulls -- does each axis's anomaly strengthen or
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   decay across the baseline.
[2026-09-21 15:15:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 130]   T5  audit: cohort composition, commensurability, cap overlaps.
